---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="How to Use Vericore" description="A practical guide to installing, analyzing, exploring, planning, and verifying with Vericore 0.7.0.">
  <main class="container page">
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">VERICORE 0.7.0</p>
      <h1>Understand. Change. Verify.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Go from a fresh installation to repository-grounded engineering decisions and a repository-bound verification boundary.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="steps">
      <article class="step"><span>01</span><div><h2>Install Vericore</h2><p>Download the current release for your platform. Released archives bundle the Java runtime for normal end-user use.</p><pre><code>vericore --version
vericore setup
vericore doctor</code></pre></div></article>
      <article class="step"><span>02</span><div><h2>Analyze a repository</h2><p>Run deterministic analysis locally. Vericore builds source, dependency, Git, architecture, and engineering signals.</p><pre><code>cd your-project
vericore analyze .
vericore reality . --json</code></pre></div></article>
      <article class="step"><span>03</span><div><h2>Explore the intelligence</h2><p>Inspect repository structure, PageRank hotspots, cycles, Git evolution, change impact, PR Intelligence, and Architecture Intelligence.</p></div></article>
      <article class="step"><span>04</span><div><h2>Ask grounded questions</h2><p>Use repository Q&amp;A to retrieve bounded evidence before answering engineering questions. AI assistance is optional.</p><pre><code>vericore repo-qa "why is PaymentService risky?" --path /path/to/repository</code></pre></div></article>
      <article class="step"><span>05</span><div><h2>Understand a change</h2><p>Use impact, PR Intelligence, architecture drift, and architecture contracts to understand affected areas and governance signals.</p><pre><code>vericore impact /path/to/repository src/main/Service.kt --json
vericore pr-intelligence /path/to/repository --json
vericore architecture-drift /path/to/repository --baseline /path/to/architecture-baseline.json --json</code></pre></div></article>
      <article class="step"><span>06</span><div><h2>Prepare the change</h2><p>Generate an evidence-backed engineering plan and a repository-bound Agent Change Contract before implementation begins.</p><pre><code>vericore prepare "add payment validation" --path /path/to/repository</code></pre></div></article>
      <article class="step"><span>07</span><div><h2>Implement, then verify</h2><p>Make the change outside Vericore, then verify against the original persisted contract. Do not replace it with a newly generated contract.</p><pre><code>vericore verify \
  --path /path/to/repository \
  --plan output/engineering-plan.json \
  --contract output/agent-change-contract.json</code></pre></div></article>
      <article class="step"><span>08</span><div><h2>Integrate with REST or MCP</h2><p>Use the local Ktor server or MCP stdio interface for trusted local/internal integrations and AI-agent workflows.</p><pre><code>vericore server --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
vericore mcp</code></pre></div></article>
    </section>

    <section class="trust">
      <h2>Local-first by design</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div><strong>Deterministic first</strong><p>Repository structure and core intelligence are produced locally and reproducibly.</p></div>
        <div><strong>AI is optional</strong><p>AI-assisted workflows can add explanation and planning without replacing repository evidence.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Persisted safety boundary</strong><p>The Agent Change Contract captures the prepared change boundary and is the basis for post-change verification.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="next"><h2>Ready to try it?</h2><p>Start with v0.7.0, inspect the generated artifacts, and follow the prepare → change → verify workflow.</p><div class="actions"><a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore/releases/latest">Download Vericore</a><a href="/docs">Read the documentation</a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page{padding:5rem 1.25rem 7rem}.hero{max-width:800px;margin-bottom:4rem}.eyebrow{font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:.78rem}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,5rem);line-height:.98;margin:.6rem 0 1.25rem}.lead{font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.7;opacity:.75}.steps{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:900px}.step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:64px 1fr;gap:1.5rem;padding:2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;background:var(--surface)}.step>span{font-weight:800;font-size:1.1rem;opacity:.45}.step h2{margin:0 0 .6rem}.step p{line-height:1.7;opacity:.78;margin:.3rem 0 1rem}.step pre{padding:1rem;border-radius:12px;overflow:auto;background:var(--code-bg,var(--surface));border:1px solid var(--border)}.trust{margin:5rem 0}.trust h2,.next h2{font-size:2rem}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}.grid>div{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px}.grid p{line-height:1.6;opacity:.75}.next{padding:2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:20px}.actions{display:flex;gap:.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.5rem}.actions a{padding:.8rem 1.1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700}.actions a:first-child{background:var(--text);color:var(--background)}
  @media(max-width:700px){.page{padding-top:3rem}.step{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:1.4rem}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hero{margin-bottom:2.5rem}}
</style>
